  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved drawings and documents: \r\rDesing and impact Statement\rHighway impact assessment\rLocation Plan\rBlock Plan\r001\r002\r003\r004\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 5 people at any one time  and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.",
    "The rear garden of the site must be accessible and usable at all times by all future occupiers for as long as the property remains in C4 Use. \r\rReason: In the interests of the residential amenity and providing a good quality form of accomodation for future residents of the HMO in accordance with the Local Plan.",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen and dinning/living room shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Within 2 months form the date of this decision five covered and secured cycle parking spaces shall be provided in a safe and convenient location within the curtilage of the application site and shall be maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of cycle parking in line with the Council's adopted standards.\r",
    "Prior to occupation, details of refuse storage facilities to be provided within the development, involving a communal container, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The facilities, namely a communal container for a HMO, shall be provided in accordance with the approved details and remain.  \r\rReason: In the interests of the residential amenity and providing a good quality form of accomodation for future residents of the HMO in accordance with the Local Plan."
  ],
